# Known Qt 6.11.2 startup finding, deliberately suppressed so the weekly
# Memcheck gate fails only on NEW memory contexts.
#
# Evidence: fork CI weekly run 42613028509 (2026-11-09, head 9d0d157) — all
# 23 suites passed and each of the 13 failing Memcheck entries reported
# "1-2 errors from 1 context": an invalid 16-byte read inside QtCore's
# QObject::connect(const char*) overloads while QApplicationPrivate::init()
# parses signal strings, before any KWin code runs (KWin frames appear only
# as callers). The same family was reproduced under the unmodified KWin
# library in the decoration-size qualification (artifacts/plasma-fusion/
# 2026-11-09-decoration-size, memory-control-baseline). The suppression was
# generated by valgrind --gen-suppressions=all in that exact lane and is
# truncated at the Qt frames so it matches every entry regardless of the
# calling test binary; the pinned libQt6Core soname keeps it from masking
# anything after a Qt update, which should be re-examined anyway.
{
   qt-6.11.2-qobject-connect-char-overloads-qbytearray-overread-at-app-init
   Memcheck:Addr16
   obj:/usr/lib64/libQt6Core.so.6.11.2
   obj:/usr/lib64/libQt6Core.so.6.11.2
   obj:/usr/lib64/libQt6Core.so.6.11.2
   obj:/usr/lib64/libQt6Core.so.6.11.2
   fun:_ZN7QObject7connectEPKS_PKcS1_S3_N2Qt14ConnectionTypeE
   fun:_ZN22QGuiApplicationPrivate4initEv
   fun:_ZN19QApplicationPrivate4initEv
}
